    "narrative": "The Austin Waves face a challenging slate today, with several starters navigating elite-level pitching, keeping our daily efficiency scores relatively suppressed. **Kyle Tucker** (51.97) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (51.04) emerge as our strongest plays, both overcoming mid-tier opposing starters through high base projections and solid order placement. **Jackson Merrill** (50.99) also warrants confidence despite a matchup against a tough arm in Misiorowski; his dynamic platoon advantage (+13%) keeps his floor well above our mandatory 40-point threshold. While **Miguel Vargas** (47.23) and **Drake Baldwin** (47.11) face sub-3.60 xERA pitchers, both retain enough upside to occupy the lineup, with **Drake Baldwin** specifically buoyed by his leadoff position, which remains vital for our Roto scoring stability.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Brayan Rocchio** (34.60), who fell well short of our 40-point floor due to his #9 spot in the batting order and a difficult matchup against Smith. While **Brayan Rocchio** possesses the requisite speed we value, his projected lack of plate appearances and the suppressed environment dictated that we preserve our game caps rather than force the start. We are also monitoring the continued absences of **Gunnar Henderson** and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** due to today\u2019s team off-days, while **Jordan Westburg** remains sidelined on the IL, further limiting our tactical flexibility. As we approach first pitch, be advised that **Liam Hicks** (40.84) is essentially at the minimum threshold; if his lineup position shifts lower than #4, he faces an immediate risk of underperforming his projection against Cole, requiring a potential pivot if the game state allows.",
